<!-- About Brother Aaron -->
<section class="content-section" id="brother-aaron">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>About Brother Aaron</h2>

        <p class="about-byline">
            <strong class="text-gold">Brother Aaron Powner</strong> &mdash; Ministering Elder &middot; Chief Author, <em>Words of Plainness</em>
        </p>

        <img
            src="/assets/images/aaron-collage.png"
            alt="Collage of Brother Aaron - teaching, traveling, and ministry moments"
            class="about-collage"
            id="aboutCollageImage"
        >

        <p>
            I spent 26 years in the classroom teaching science to young people&mdash;helping them
            understand the natural world and discover the joy of asking good questions. Now,
            in what some might call retirement, I've found that the questions I most want to
            explore are the ones science alone can't answer.
        </p>

        <p>
            I'm an ordained Elder in the Melchizedek Priesthood of The Church of Jesus Christ
            of Latter-day Saints. My faith was shaped by years of study, service, and a mission
            to Argentina that changed how I see the world. But this ministry isn't about
            promoting one denomination over another&mdash;it's about Jesus Christ and the common
            ground shared by all who seek Him.
        </p>

        <p>
            Within this ministry I carry the title of Ministering Elder. I hold it not as a
            rank but as a description of the work itself&mdash;to minister, in the plain and
            ongoing sense of that word, to whoever God sets in my path. When it comes to the
            writings gathered here, I answer to a second title: Chief Author. My brother Jim
            labors beside me, and the heart of this work is shared between us; but the governing
            pen, and the accountability that comes with holding it, rests with me. For more
            information, feel free to read the
            <a href="/chapters/01-introduction/" class="text-gold">first chapter of my writings</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
            Today, my wife and I travel in our RV, meeting people wherever we go. I host
            interfaith discussions in VR Chat, create music as part of the Powner Method,
            and write with the goal of making deep truths accessible. If you ever cross paths
            with a bald, bearded fellow talking about faith in a coffee shop or campground,
            it might be me.
        </p>

